json5p/code
description: JSON5 with pointers — json5/code extended with the pointer layer
- >
  **json5p** is this project's own language —
  [json5/code](::language:01-Concretes_2:06-json5_code) plus the **pointer layer**, and nothing
  else. A `*` pointer makes a SHARED edge where JSON and JSON5 could only copy, and an `&` anchor
  writes the reverse edge. JSON ⊂ JSON5 ⊂ json5p — every JSON5 code is also valid json5p:
- !!<format: text/x-json5p> |
  {
    pets: [
      {name: 'Rex', species: 'dog'},
      {name: 'Whiskers', species: 'cat'},
    ],
    feline: *"pets: 1",              // a pointer — the SAME node as pets position 1
    boss: &": chief" {name: 'Rex'},  // an anchor — this node ALSO lives at `: chief`
  }
- >
  As in JSON5, a json5p code is one value — structured or scalar — and comments may accompany it
  anywhere between tokens. See the subchapters below:
- *: 00-json5p_structured
- *: 01-json5p_scalar
- *..:06-json5_code:02-json5_comment
- *..:06-json5_code
